Subject: Object allocation helpers that take the function's bytecode instead of its frame

What this does
  - `qjs_aot_object_template_b` and `qjs_aot_object_fill_b` are `qjs_aot_object_template`
    and `qjs_aot_object_fill` with the function's bytecode in place of its frame; the
    frame forms call them.
  - A compiled function with no frame (one that calls or allocates) can then build and
    fill an object literal. Nothing else changes.

Why we need it
  An object literal in a recursive builder (a tree constructor) kept the function
  framed, and a framed recursion needs the interpreter's frame size per level plus the
  C frame, so it could not reach the interpreter's depth.

